s a matrix whose respective columns are the coordinates of the vectors of $B$ relative to the basis $S.$ \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124981 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3450a5c8-0638-5f54-91c6-f0904adbd73b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=-3,$ $b=0,$ and $c=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321543} {:answer/id #uuid "7d55ebf2-a70f-58b2-bda2-03e326fed525" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=0,$ $b=0,$ and $c=1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322131} {:answer/id #uuid "b5524681-77e7-579d-a437-18f18838ecfa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=-5,$ $b=4,$ and $c=1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322560} {:answer/id #uuid "bcd8971c-8b76-5fff-83b4-0341d34ab0bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=-3,$ $b=-1,$ and $c=1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322611} {:answer/id #uuid "c652602d-b564-5dd8-957a-b3260e0d934a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=-3,$ $b=0,$ and $c=4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322682}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=-3,$ $b=-1,$ and $c=1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322611} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0b7f4ae-f69c-5c98-b0a6-78974d07ef20" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323512}] :question/id #uuid "62a8923e-9667-58a1-b193-1a3c8d5a2238" :question/math-academy-id "q-36400" :question/problem "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}$ be a basis of ${R}^{3}$ and let $S$ be the standard basis of ${R}^{3}.$ What are the values of $a,b,$ and $c$ if \n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nand the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is \n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=\\begin{bmatrix}a & -5 & 0 \\\\ 4 & b & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & c\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall  that the standard basis of ${R}^{3}$ consists of the vectors ${e}_{1},{e}_{2},$ and ${e}_{3},$ given by\n\n$$\n{e}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{e}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{e}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe components of the vectors in $B$ are just the coordinates relative to the standard basis:\n\n$$\n[{b}_{1}]_{S}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,[{b}_{2}]_{S}=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,[{b}_{3}]_{S}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is a matrix whose respective columns are the coordinates of the vectors of $B$ relative to the basis $S.$ \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFinally, $a=-3,$ $b=-1,$ and $c=1.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247325 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21ec7e52-e1a4-5f34-94a4-4a2a10999dce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244611} {:answer/id #uuid "441eae26-77fe-5f8a-bb28-967e73a779aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244909} {:answer/id #uuid "70483028-a920-5132-98b7-edf06a15cdcd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245318} {:answer/id #uuid "bdd78156-1002-5585-a3e4-b242754a30c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246005} {:answer/id #uuid "c075d9dd-02eb-5dd8-9bd9-984020c932af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246027}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246005} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5c93fe6-cd76-5169-ad0c-593bc8dd1824" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246878}] :question/id #uuid "aa182112-8f71-5fbc-8bf6-38e37fb6643c" :question/math-academy-id "q-113115" :question/problem "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and let $S$ be the standard basis of ${R}^{2}.$ \nFind the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{B\\to S}$ from $B$ to $S$ if \n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall  that the standard basis of ${R}^{2}$ consists of the vectors ${e}_{1}$ and ${e}_{2},$ given by\n\n$$\n{e}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{e}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe components of the vectors of $B$ are just the coordinates relative to the standard basis:\n\n$$\n[{b}_{1}]_{S}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,[{b}_{2}]_{S}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is a matrix whose respective columns are the coordinates of the vectors of $B$ relative to the basis $S.$ \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377844 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c4d259b5-915f-51f3-b82a-a4a9da133e01" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=0,$ $b=-1,$ and $c=-5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377846} {:answer/id #uuid "0d4211cf-c344-5620-b95d-15c507cdd614" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=3,$ $b=4,$ and $c=3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377847} {:answer/id #uuid "f98495bd-241d-5544