wer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 11\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394295} :answer-field/id #uuid "8055db6f-b8ff-53ba-9dfb-f141126526ea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394292}] :question/id #uuid "62dadad6-bc72-59c3-b335-faab5922669e" :question/math-academy-id "q-81847" :question/problem "Let $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and let $S$ be the standard basis of ${R}^{2}.$ \nFind the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{B\\to S}$ from $B$ to $S$ if \n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 11\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall  that the standard basis of ${R}^{2}$ consists of the vectors ${e}_{1}$ and ${e}_{2},$ given by\n\n$$\n{e}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{e}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe components of the vectors of $B$ are just the coordinates relative to the standard basis:\n\n$$\n[{b}_{1}]_{S}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix},\\,[{b}_{2}]_{S}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 11\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is a matrix whose respective columns are the coordinates of the vectors of $B$ relative to the basis $S.$ \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 11\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186394298 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "026f1607-4c08-5aa9-bf58-cfb40b330832" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=7,$ $b=0,$ and $c=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394300} {:answer/id #uuid "3baad480-b3b5-5d93-a51a-4fd762b5a712" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=0,$ $b=7,$ and $c=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394301} {:answer/id #uuid "d0c36859-9ec2-5784-9edb-98a495812bcc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=1,$ $b=-2,$ and $c=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 1759