inates of the vectors of $B$ relative to the basis $S.$ \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFinally, $a=7,$ $b=0,$ and $c=0.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416599 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26ea652b-6e02-523c-b2ba-b95e1959da46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=-1,$ $b=8,$ and $c=5.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416534} {:answer/id #uuid "6615ba74-1fb7-56ad-903d-4b77c16b3dd6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=7,$ $b=5,$ and $c=8.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416550} {:answer/id #uuid "6c73720e-ba56-5223-a2a5-3a7a43ab5d38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=8,$ $b=5,$ and $c=7.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416552} {:answer/id #uuid "7a0f28c3-3134-5225-add6-826343463b74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=-1,$ $b=7,$ and $c=5.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416557} {:answer/id #uuid "dcc6f90c-1011-5415-bdbb-61b071aed3be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=8,$ $b=-1,$ and $c=7.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416578}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=8,$ $b=5,$ and $c=7.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416552} :answer-field/id #uuid "8192819f-c781-5fbc-98ce-44030ec1bb27" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416592}] :question/id #uuid "9a2d831b-a3f1-5313-8aee-60f8e3a93edc" :question/math-academy-id "q-81852" :question/problem "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}$ be a basis of ${R}^{3}$ and let $S$ be the standard basis of ${R}^{3}.$ What are the values of $a,b,$ and $c$ if \n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nand the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is \n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & a & 7 \\\\ -1 & 4 & b \\\\ 4 & c & -9\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall  that the standard basis of ${R}^{3}$ consists of the vectors ${e}_{1},{e}_{2},$ and ${e}_{3},$ given by\n\n$$\n{e}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{e}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{e}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe components of the vectors in $B$ are just the coordinates relative to the standard basis:\n\n$$\n[{b}_{1}]_{S}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,[{b}_{2}]_{S}=\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix},\\,[{b}_{3}]_{S}=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is a matrix whose respective columns are the coordinates of the vectors of $B$ relative to the basis $S.$ \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 8 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 7 & -9\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFinally, $a=8,$ $b=5,$ and $c=7.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416601 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08510d9c-0008-5b50-b913-170c103ba9c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416526} {:answer/id #uuid "177497c8-e142-5d9e-abc1-becbb9a39472" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ -9 & 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416530} {:answer/id #uuid "22bb294d-e537-5a35-8529-6eae6486a39b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-9 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416532} {:answer/id #uuid "367a8769-cd6a-5b95-9967-7c0f59ab154d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & -9 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416536} {:answer/id #uuid "b3066f3f-5c4f-536c-8694-1e282ae85a94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ -6 & 9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416571}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ -6 & 9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416571} :answer-field/id #uuid "987253ee-4461-5046-b1db-ce4100ac59cc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416593}] :question/id #uuid "b28dc41f-f44a-5439-b028-42214a679df4" :question/math-academy-id "q-36402" :question/problem "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and let $S$ be the standard basis of ${R}^{2}.$ \nFind the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{B\\to S}$ from $B$ to $S$ if \n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall  that the standard basis of ${R}^{2}$ consists of the vectors ${e}_{1}$ and ${e}_{2},$ given by\n\n$$\n{e}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{e}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe components of the vectors of $B$ are just the coordinates relative to the standard basis:\n\n$$\n[{b}_{1}]_{S}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\text{ and }\\,[{b}_{2}]_{S}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is a matrix whose respective columns are the coordinates of the vectors of $B$ relative to the basis $S.$ \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ -6 & 9\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416603 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07838b3a-5d21-5d4b-96ed-ad6dca8941c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416525} {:answer/id #uuid "16853ab7-760d-5058-8e30-4207c809785e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416528} {:answer/id #uuid "87e78e9b-fea5-57d2-9ca3-96814468f5f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416560} {:answer/id #uuid "b9b03fb3-ebd1-50f3-8cee-c5c60249d1de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416573} {:answer/id #uuid "c80a8828-4df2-559c-b9ff-6f138f31421c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ -5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416575}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416528} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c86502d-b8b8-5473-bf1a-5d435069f0e5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416586}] :question/id #uuid "d6ffc405-f81c-5336-ad94-25ea55190ac1" :question/math-academy-id "q-113342" :question/problem "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and let $S$ be the standard basis of ${R}^{2}.$ \nFind the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{B\\to S}$ from $B$ to $S$ if \n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall  that the standard basis of ${R}^{2}$ consists of the vectors ${e}_{1}$ and ${e}_{2},$ given by\n\n$$\n{e}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{e}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe components of the vectors of $B$ are just the coordinates relative to the standard basis:\n\n$$\n[{b}_{1}]_{S}=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,[{b}_{2}]_{S}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is a matrix whose respective columns are the coordinates of the vectors of $B$ relative to the basis $S.$ \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426286 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33773b31-42d5-5b22-b69d-d51cba57075a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=7,$ $b=3,$ and $c=2.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426274} {:answer/id #uuid "38d68fa8-7de7-5c1e-a154-a690cae0ed7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=0,$ $b=2,$ and $c=5.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426275} {:answer/id #uuid "4c86e4c7-bde7-518f-883c-d6733741d589" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=7,$ $b=2,$ and $c=3.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426276} {:answer/id #uuid "90c0ac77-fbcb-52ce-b243-0e75ec356a91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=-1,$ $b=-4,$ and $c=2.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426279} {:answer/id #uuid "b56f736f-e3af-523b-9386-b38726eccfb7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=0,$ $b=5,$ and $c=2.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426280}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=0,$ $b=2,$ and $c=5.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426275} :answer-field/id #uuid "9be8ac92-24b2-5071-9ee2-8d0a8572a03d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426284}] :question/id #uuid "b83d51a4-64e8-5d15-b4eb-1a14ddbe497b" :question/math-academy-id "q-81851" :question/problem "Let $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}$ be a basis of ${R}^{3}$ and let $S$ be the standard basis of ${R}^{3}.$ What are the values of $a,b,$ and $c$ if \n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nand the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is \n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=\\begin{bmatrix}a & 3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 1 & b \\\\ 7 & c & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall  that the standard basis of ${R}^{3}$ consists of the vectors ${e}_{1},{e}_{2},$ and ${e}_{3},$ given by\n\n$$\n{e}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{e}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{e}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe components of the vectors in $B$ are just the coordinates relative to the standard basis:\n\n$$\n[{b}_{1}]_{S}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix},\\,[{b}_{2}]_{S}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix},\\,[{b}_{3}]_{S}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is a matrix whose respective columns are the coordinates of the vectors of $B$ relative to the basis $S.$ \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 7 & 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFinally, $a=0,$ $b=2,$ and $c=5.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434950 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16bee97f-7038-5e53-805e-c034d4f9aa98" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434934} {:answer/id #uuid "53b1d470-247b-548b-b13d-bc66e9449c39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434937} {:answer/id #uuid "7251156a-c21f-5adb-9ff9-bd33a768f1d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434938} {:answer/id #uuid "bdb98ddb-73a6-5232-b35f-26201c89674c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434943}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434937} :answer-field/id #uuid "99aa8a6d-990b-5e61-8b84-2888eb56d9f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434949}] :question/id #uuid "75d038ad-b39f-5c52-a2ee-ada0d3f5df01" :question/math-academy-id "q-113116" :question/problem "Let $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and let $S$ be the standard basis of ${R}^{2}.$ \nFind the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{B\\to S}$ from $B$ to $S$ if \n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall  that the standard basis of ${R}^{2}$ consists of the vectors ${e}_{1}$ and ${e}_{2},$ given by\n\n$$\n{e}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{e}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe components of the vectors of $B$ are just the coordinates relative to the standard basis:\n\n$$\n[{b}_{1}]_{S}=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,[{b}_{2}]_{S}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is a matrix whose respective columns are the coordinates of the vectors of $B$ relative to the basis $S.$ \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Change-of-Coordinates Matrix When One of the Bases is the Standard Basis"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124493 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124306 :question/id #uuid "6c5b5534-2082-593e-af07-df83497ea84c" :question/math-academy-id "e-4835" :question/problem "The change-of-coordinates matrix from the basis $\\mathcal{B}$ to the basis $\\mathcal{C}$ is given by \n![](images/46/4676de86bd5b4bc2a8e1d6a9432379d0769163113913137f8143a71eb16e8240.svg)\nFind the change-of-coordinates matrix from $\\mathcal{C}$ to $\\mathcal{B}.$" :question/worked-solution "The change-of-coordinates matrix from $\\mathcal{C}$ to $\\mathcal{B}$ is the inverse of the change-of-coordinates matrix from $\\mathcal{B}$ to $\\mathcal{C}.$ Therefore, we simply need to find the inverse of the given matrix.\n\nComputing the inverse of $P_{\\small\\mathcal{B}\\to\\mathcal{C}},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{C\\to B} & ={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -6 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-4)\\cdot 5-(-6)\\cdot 3}\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 6 \\\\ -3 & -4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =(-\\frac{1}{2})\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}5 & 6 \\\\ -3 & -4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{5}{2} & -3 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2} & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "23b6a85e-e1de-590c-84d2-379052b1b9f3" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124914 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20f58787-8399-5ca4-a011-8a6df79512f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -\\frac{5}{3}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434935} {:answer/id #uuid "91a0872a-5de1-5bcf-bf96-cd7b7f09e1c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -\\frac{5}{3}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434940} {:answer/id #uuid "c3bfcb95-4180-5b13-9c4f-4eca7f2802a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -\\frac{5}{3} \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434944} {:answer/id #uuid "da5b45fe-6463-5cf0-bb39-9946f196f0dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -\\frac{5}{3} \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434946} {:answer/id #uuid "ef95b44c-9f4a-5eb2-8a32-5755e8f3f15d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & \\frac{5}{3}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434947}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -\\frac{5}{3} \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434944} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd4a1d79-e29c-55e2-9104-304e27e73d47" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122084}] :question/id #uuid "3bc8c503-4f0a-519e-810b-af533bd26af8" :question/math-academy-id "q-35793" :question/problem "The change-of-coordinates matrix from the basis $B$ to the basis $C$ is given by \n${P}_{B\\to C}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -5 \\\\ -6 & 9\\end{bmatrix}.$\nFind the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B$  ." :question/worked-solution "The change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B$ is the inverse of the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$ Therefore, we simply need to find the inverse of the given matrix.\n\nComputing the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to C}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{C\\to B} & ={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -5 \\\\ -6 & 9\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\cdot 9-(-5)\\cdot (-6)}\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-3}\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -\\frac{5}{3} \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124915 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ccc4635-e273-5882-a5f3-8657d632bfa3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -7 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321494} {:answer/id #uuid "7c2b87ce-54b3-5e6b-afc5-1a23f2dc0532" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 7 \\\\ 3 & -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322123} {:answer/id #uuid "867651a0-ba37-5806-8c23-f13d4305e3af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 3 \\\\ -7 & -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322215} {:answer/id #uuid "c48604f7-6382-589a-98ec-22494e2380a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -5 \\\\ 4 & 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322672} {:answer/id #uuid "f1226200-4ad1-5b6f-9a6a-1fe6b195fcdb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 3 \\\\ -7 & 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323045}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -7 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321494} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b91185f-8c4c-5c85-bb18-da7ea9550ad9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323411}] :question/id #uuid "51bd98dc-1e1e-5c5c-9609-7609b0be859e" :question/math-academy-id "q-35799" :question/problem "The change-of-coordinates matrix from the basis $C$ to the basis $B$ is given by\n${P}_{C\\to B}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 7 \\\\ -3 & -4\\end{bmatrix}.$ Find the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$  ." :question/worked-solution "The change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$ is the inverse of the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B.$ Therefore, we simply need to find the inverse of the given matrix.\n\nComputing the inverse of ${P}_{C\\to B}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to C} & ={P}_{C\\to B}^{-1} \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 7 \\\\ -3 & -4\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5\\cdot (-4)-7\\cdot (-3)}\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -7 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -7 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -7 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247348 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46d042fb-ea8c-5358-83cf-1e4a627e5b20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244944} {:answer/id #uuid "588ad8ca-e31e-5635-ab44-a4f63f99cf44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245095} {:answer/id #uuid "61ba8fe7-4234-546e-8a75-79c552e5f498" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245170} {:answer/id #uuid "983d7c0b-09f0-51f9-866a-6774f9397b84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245664} {:answer/id #uuid "c15672bc-2fed-5ee4-a277-6611b8be7b19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} & -1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246037}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} & -1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246037} :answer-field/id #uuid "597a0b46-6ae7-5a49-9065-089e272347b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246705}] :question/id #uuid "d86d7038-3836-547b-82af-27a9e8b49db8" :question/math-academy-id "q-113411" :question/problem "The change-of-coordinates matrix from the basis $C$ to the basis $B$ is given by\n${P}_{C\\to B}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.$ Find the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$" :question/worked-solution "The change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$ is the inverse of the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B.$ Therefore, we simply need to find the inverse of the given matrix.\n\nComputing the inverse of ${P}_{C\\to B}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to C} & ={P}_{C\\to B}^{-1} \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4\\cdot (-1)-(-2)\\cdot 1}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =(-\\frac{1}{2})\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} & -1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247349 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1006640e-9d75-599c-877c-96d359a3fa69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 3 \\\\ 9 & 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244462} {:answer/id #uuid "42160313-d20d-5459-8d6f-cbc3455b020c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -9 \\\\ -3 & 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244891} {:answer/id #uuid "757412d1-09bb-588e-8eab-d5175af0ed23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -3 \\\\ -9 & 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245359} {:answer/id #uuid "d2e37099-402c-5b14-93b8-cb301499b55a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -3 \\\\ -9 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246190} {:answer/id #uuid "e1d65427-e485-5f40-ae92-d2540533f8bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9 & -7 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246323}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -3 \\\\ -9 & 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245359} :answer-field/id #uuid "a490c9f0-7a30-569b-b5f7-30e0b6190adc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246838}] :question/id #uuid "6524c152-aeba-5139-803b-30e61293f48c" :question/math-academy-id "q-113413" :question/problem "The change-of-coordinates matrix from the basis $C$ to the basis $B$ is given by\n${P}_{C\\to B}=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 3 \\\\ 9 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.$ Find the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$  ." :question/worked-solution "The change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$ is the inverse of the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B.$ Therefore, we simply need to find the inverse of the given matrix.\n\nComputing the inverse of ${P}_{C\\to B}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to C} & ={P}_{C\\to B}^{-1} \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 3 \\\\ 9 & 4\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7\\cdot 4-3\\cdot 9}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -3 \\\\ -9 & 7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}4 & -3 \\\\ -9 & 7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -3 \\\\ -9 & 7\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351380 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01517329-3e28-5805-9aac-584f93b1c3a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & -7 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348463} {:answer/id #uuid "7366ef02-a1d3-52aa-8a52-8f56ad1cbc7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 7 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349508} {:answer/id #uuid "7953ac21-87d0-5f72-9103-11cc5e921515" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 7 \\\\ -3 & -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349566} {:answer/id #uuid "d7d93798-cb62-5237-98c5-12c645b92461" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & -3 \\\\ -7 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350337} {:answer/id #uuid "e43d5839-5161-5f91-9c65-2cdc6114d39b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -3 \\\\ 7 & -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350450}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 7 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349508} :answer-field/id #uuid "6039748f-1eb1-57b4-8f7e-0fdd49400251" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350866}] :question/id #uuid "0cf13df2-1351-5dd8-a600-8ae95cd08849" :question/math-academy-id "q-81855" :question/problem "The change-of-coordinates matrix from the basis $B$ to the basis $C$ is given by \n${P}_{B\\to C}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -7 \\\\ 3 & -5\\end{bmatrix}.$\nFind the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B$  ." :question/worked-solution "The change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B$ is the inverse of the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$ Therefore, we simply need to find the inverse of the given matrix.\n\nComputing the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to C}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{C\\to B} & ={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -7 \\\\ 3 & -5\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4\\cdot (-5)-(-7)\\cdot 3}\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 7 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 7 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 7 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351381 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1370479a-3aa2-5980-8b5d-bf80c36b0345" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 5 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348615} {:answer/id #uuid "2e96fe0a-510e-5876-8dc4-ed532f43fcde" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & -7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348859} {:answer/id #uuid "3c48ef2d-d23d-543c-abd7-95d4f593804f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 \\\\ 5 & -7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348991} {:answer/id #uuid "7142e1a4-9ef4-5efe-9846-55db85ffeba7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 3 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349491} {:answer/id #uuid "d1f0a9f2-4cf4-5bc7-9365-98f05029ba07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350290}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 3 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349491} :answer-field/id #uuid "94f26393-b3e3-57a4-b231-854253f6fc7c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350962}] :question/id #uuid "15b0301b-0195-533a-ac3f-0f147e15a6e9" :question/math-academy-id "q-81856" :question/problem "The change-of-coordinates matrix from the basis $B$ to the basis $C$ is given by \n${P}_{B\\to C}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 7\\end{bmatrix}.$ \nFind the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B$  ." :question/worked-solution "The change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B$ is the inverse of the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$ Therefore, we simply need to find the inverse of the given matrix.\n\nComputing the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to C}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{C\\to B} & ={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 7\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot 7-3\\cdot 5}\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}7 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 3 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375741 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c68bf4be-203e-571e-a616-048718c4f570" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -\\frac{3}{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375743} {:answer/id #uuid "871ce294-0184-52a0-8c4a-f6301da569dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375744} {:answer/id #uuid "ade19cd5-9bd4-5ab5-bc23-04a1a99d9ab5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2} & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375745} {:answer/id #uuid "a36bb172-8f9c-51ba-a51e-897afcc18550" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{3} & -1 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375746} {:answer/id #uuid "436f56e8-8781-5c3a-b319-5103d45dbc85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375747}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2} & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375745} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8c1bc41-fa12-5f31-9cf0-0ba1e1bb8d0b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375742}] :question/id #uuid "8573e369-ef36-53f6-af79-2a6af4ca823d" :question/math-academy-id "q-113414" :question/problem "The change-of-coordinates matrix from the basis $C$ to the basis $B$ is given by\n${P}_{C\\to B}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.$ Find the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$  ." :question/worked-solution "The change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$ is the inverse of the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B.$ Therefore, we simply need to find the inverse of the given matrix.\n\nComputing the inverse of ${P}_{C\\to B}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to C} & ={P}_{C\\to B}^{-1} \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot 4-2\\cdot 3}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}4 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2} & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386675 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "919eb1e9-2f4b-56b6-88e5-3859874737bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386677} {:answer/id #uuid "90eeb8b6-e3b5-53db-a5fe-f9746d4ccb88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386678} {:answer/id #uuid "b872cd7b-0659-5c54-8111-e27c28adc0d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386679} {:answer/id #uuid "bbdc24c8-890c-5fc5-a78e-92d48b19a269" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386680} {:answer/id #uuid "e9bec6ef-0b83-555d-8bfe-9ff77d315986" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386681}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386677} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f7670fd-c5bc-51f7-98ba-bd3ac9cdc072" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386676}] :question/id #uuid "0e492abb-150e-5b29-ab40-6db339f73d6b" :question/math-academy-id "q-113415" :question/problem "The change-of-coordinates matrix from the basis $B$ to the basis $C$ is given by \n${P}_{B\\to C}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{2} & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.$\nFind the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B$  ." :question/worked-solution "The change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B$ is the inverse of the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$ Therefore, we simply need to find the inverse of the given matrix.\n\nComputing the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to C}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{C\\to B} & ={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{2} & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot (-1)-1\\cdot (-2)}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & \\frac{3}{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & \\frac{3}{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186394305 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cb6b89d9-5ecc-523c-9fe0-a98270e715c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & \\frac{2}{3} \\\\ -3 & \\frac{5}{3}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394307} {:answer/id #uuid "b48cca5a-57d5-5e3e-85fc-5f7371b9a168" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ -\\frac{2}{3} & -\\frac{5}{3}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394308} {:answer/id #uuid "ebadf3ae-54e1-5e2d-ac3c-70c2f31c63ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{5}{3} & \\frac{2}{3} \\\\ -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394309} {:answer/id #uuid "0f308fd4-f8a6-5e5f-860e-48792c8fbbdb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{5}{3} & -\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394310} {:answer/id #uuid "00d59288-f8b5-5054-8c1f-b5518246d305" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ 3 & \\frac{5}{3}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394311}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ 3 & \\frac{5}{3}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394311} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d1bd593-f01f-5378-b1fe-6d41f9f01e52" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394306}] :question/id #uuid "a27a3c1e-ad3c-56e4-aa1a-d2aedbc7058d" :question/math-academy-id "q-81859" :question/problem "The change-of-coordinates matrix from the basis $C$ to the basis $B$ is given by\n${P}_{C\\to B}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 2 \\\\ -9 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.$ Find the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$  ." :question/worked-solution "The change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$ is the inverse of the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B.$ Therefore, we simply need to find the inverse of the given matrix.\n\nComputing the inverse of ${P}_{C\\to B}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to C} & ={P}_{C\\to B}^{-1} \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 2 \\\\ -9 & -3\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5\\cdot (-3)-2\\cdot (-9)}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -2 \\\\ 9 & 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -2 \\\\ 9 & 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ 3 & \\frac{5}{3}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186394312 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ceb0e647-cc62-5520-96d0-a62ea4b7b70a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -9 \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394314} {:answer/id #uuid "91a2a780-e072-57b3-a258-6f82c21f34c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -3 \\\\ 9 & -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394315} {:answer/id #uuid "b5dc2ed0-ef85-5f46-8701-75a045762a06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 9 \\\\ -3 & 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394316} {:answer/id #uuid "64865972-6c7f-5e6a-914f-7ca5dabf44da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 9 \\\\ -3 & -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394317} {:answer/id #uuid "e7efc8a7-50e9-5361-a425-938758af899c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 3 \\\\ -9 & 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394318}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 9 \\\\ -3 & -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394317} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ec1a78f-b951-5ee0-943b-80972e450245" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394313}] :question/id #uuid "3af65f58-119f-54f0-83bf-1e885de9ae50" :question/math-academy-id "q-81860" :question/problem "The change-of-coordinates matrix from the basis $C$ to the basis $B$ is given by\n${P}_{C\\to B}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 9 \\\\ -3 & -7\\end{bmatrix}.$ Find the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$  ." :question/worked-solution "The change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$ is the inverse of the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B.$ Therefore, we simply need to find the inverse of the given matrix.\n\nComputing the inverse of ${P}_{C\\to B}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to C} & ={P}_{C\\to B}^{-1} \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 9 \\\\ -3 & -7\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4\\cdot (-7)-9\\cdot (-3)}\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & -9 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-7 & -9 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 9 \\\\ -3 & -4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416600 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a7deef8-19c9-5a99-beb9-30ea6eec4a82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{4} & -1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416535} {:answer/id #uuid "3e6f0908-6c0d-5c24-87f5-821d61c33178" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416540} {:answer/id #uuid "90c78f39-cbdd-5735-93c9-853cf06b1825" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416563} {:answer/id #uuid "aa836202-b0e6-521c-8443-a083a03ee71c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416568} {:answer/id #uuid "b249e81c-9b0f-550d-b583-627092bcf567" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416570}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416563} :answer-field/id #uuid "04d718c2-a214-5ef1-82b5-17f86c63db92" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416584}] :question/id #uuid "a26dc326-54d9-5ae2-96c3-423118f36c64" :question/math-academy-id "q-113409" :question/problem "The change-of-coordinates matrix from the basis $B$ to the basis $C$ is given by \n${P}_{B\\to C}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\nFind the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B$  ." :question/worked-solution "The change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B$ is the inverse of the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$ Therefore, we simply need to find the inverse of the given matrix.\n\nComputing the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to C}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{C\\to B} & ={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot (-3)}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416605 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60bc38dd-e04b-53b1-91b2-6bb378d41837" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416549} {:answer/id #uuid "71d81bba-103c-52d1-9ba7-ba524273847c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 5 \\\\ -3 & -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416555} {:answer/id #uuid "7fde4386-2338-52c7-a292-c73f0e034d10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -5 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416559} {:answer/id #uuid "9cf2c82b-0f69-5967-94d6-03180ca54721" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -5 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416565} {:answer/id #uuid "ca7a94f0-7d2a-56ba-bb59-168b33d3bb36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416576}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -5 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416559} :answer-field/id #uuid "2cc46cdd-beb2-5ee4-a2a8-1259b1fb90ca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416588}] :question/id #uuid "df33f267-a622-55d4-b6ca-07fa624cf0e9" :question/math-academy-id "q-113410" :question/problem "The change-of-coordinates matrix from the basis $C$ to the basis $B$ is given by\n${P}_{C\\to B}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.$ Find the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$  ." :question/worked-solution "The change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$ is the inverse of the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B.$ Therefore, we simply need to find the inverse of the given matrix.\n\nComputing the inverse of ${P}_{C\\to B}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to C} & ={P}_{C\\to B}^{-1} \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4\\cdot 4-5\\cdot 3}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -5 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}4 & -5 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -5 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416606 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "172c82bc-392e-5ec7-9deb-ddba9ffa9f17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 6 \\\\ -4 & -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416529} {:answer/id #uuid "6a9c0465-d9d9-5b77-b798-d3d852db486e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -5 \\\\ 5 & -6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416551} {:answer/id #uuid "6c8d2ddf-0d76-50dd-b764-f107e2c723e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 5 \\\\ -5 & -6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416553} {:answer/id #uuid "6fb38a3d-724f-59ef-90ac-504aa9672e91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 5 \\\\ -5 & 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416554} {:answer/id #uuid "e2f776f7-8d29-51a7-9c76-2fe228c44b24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 5 \\\\ -5 & -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416579}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 5 \\\\ -5 & -6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416553} :answer-field/id #uuid "74971671-dff2-5641-9515-43efb29ddf1c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416591}] :question/id #uuid "f1424ed2-0052-5fff-908d-b6551bfbb11a" :question/math-academy-id "q-81857" :question/problem "The change-of-coordinates matrix from the basis $C$ to the basis $B$ is given by\n${P}_{C\\to B}=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & -5 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.$ Find the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$  ." :question/worked-solution "The change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$ is the inverse of the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B.$ Therefore, we simply need to find the inverse of the given matrix.\n\nComputing the inverse of ${P}_{C\\to B}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to C} & ={P}_{C\\to B}^{-1} \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & -5 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-6)\\cdot 4-(-5)\\cdot 5}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 5 \\\\ -5 & -6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}4 & 5 \\\\ -5 & -6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 5 \\\\ -5 & -6\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Using the Invertibility Property of the Change-of-Coordinates Matrix"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124494 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124307 :question/id #uuid "0929855b-0310-5c87-8cff-cc2faa8a5ae0" :question/math-academy-id "e-4837" :question/problem "Let ![](images/07/076634439afec4c0e4fb0a443d88163245269988e323ddb9d83d1a4a1b18139e.svg) and ![](images/b2/b2fd30034f45fb2d8b06f2697f137c93de21942822b08193c3e640ef51d4e7c0.svg) be bases of $\\mathbb{R}^2.$ Find the change-of-coordinates matrix from $\\mathcal{B}$ to $\\mathcal{C}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $\\mathcal{B}$ and $\\mathcal{C}$ as $\\{ \\mathbf{b}_1,\\mathbf{b}_2 \\}$ and $\\{ \\mathbf{c}_1,\\mathbf{c}_2 \\},$ respectively.\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $\\mathcal{B}$ to $\\mathcal{C}$ is a matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors of $\\mathcal{B}$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{C}.$\n\nSo, we need to find the coordinates of $\\mathbf{b}_1$ and $\\mathbf{b}_2$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{C}.$ We can do this simultaneously by considering the matrix\n![](images/dd/dd733ebebc7131eb2762e6e98e1d14d07a730e5e37657c639ae9cc46be123ee2.svg)\n\nNow, we simply reduce the left-hand side to reduced row-echelon form using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 7 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 13\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 4 & 22 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 13\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the right-hand side, we obtain the change-of-coordinates matrix from $\\mathcal{B}$ to $\\mathcal{C}.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to C}= & \\begin{bmatrix}\\,4 & 22 \\\\ \\,1 & 13\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f989cbaf-2d99-5267-8864-48a48db2d535" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124916 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20235027-ad55-59fe-b1e5-b1705f888d17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416531} {:answer/id #uuid "4dd79918-775f-5123-b336-42017be04695" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416543} {:answer/id #uuid "7928c32a-4f5a-5fbd-ab9a-645a98853355" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416556} {:answer/id #uuid "7c7fa779-b799-54a8-ad4c-a9e9dcea93d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416558} {:answer/id #uuid "ead71fbb-62b9-559f-94fe-b5cd728b52ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416581}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416543} :answer-field/id #uuid "249ce60b-00ae-5912-900c-fca2a8f69bfe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416587}] :question/id #uuid "f27d85cd-7d1d-52da-929b-4fa8b04cc954" :question/math-academy-id "q-35805" :question/problem "Let $B={\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}}$  be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and let $S$ be the standard basis of ${R}^{2}.$ Find the change-of-coordinates matrix from $S$ to $B.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ and $S$ as ${{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ and ${{e}_{1},{e}_{2}}$, respectively. Recall that the standard basis of ${R}^{2}$ consists of the vectors\n\n$$\n{e}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{e}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $S$ to $B$ is a matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors of $S$ relative to the basis $B.$\n\nHence, we need to find the coordinates of ${e}_{1}$ and ${e}_{2}$ relative to the basis $B.$ We can do this simultaneously by considering the matrix\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}| & | & | & | \\\\ {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} & {e}_{1} & {e}_{2} \\\\ | & | & | & |\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we simply reduce the left-hand side to reduced row-echelon form using Gaussian elimination: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the right-hand side, we obtain the change-of-coordinates matrix from $S$ to $B.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{P}_{S\\to B}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124974 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a3c94a24-ce00-57d7-87d8-2d894ed9c1b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 7 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122445} {:answer/id #uuid "dbf7f23e-7437-5d9a-9025-ec64c7d011ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -7 \\\\ 5 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122446} {:answer/id #uuid "125a095d-a34d-59e2-88a8-bc20f5b0098d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122447} {:answer/id #uuid "2eca85bc-0d78-50da-84b4-c75bdff15840" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 1 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122448} {:answer/id #uuid "588d5e51-a23b-568e-bc20-379baf427c3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 7 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122449}] :answer-field/id #uuid "fdcd652c-4855-54f5-b6c4-a78a37b32e07" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122444} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c28c046-8359-5ce5-97a2-d07ed718e82a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -7 \\\\ 5 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391972} {:answer/id #uuid "a7da6dd7-b4a2-5527-b8b0-d7b7c036a752" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 1 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391973} {:answer/id #uuid "8609130e-bb71-54ff-89ea-c6f4ca217543" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 7 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391974} {:answer/id #uuid "aa2d4e5f-8518-54ef-9650-5f530cd0010a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 7 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391975} {:answer/id #uuid "a97992e7-99d1-5b0d-bf18-21127d13f345" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391976}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 7 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391974} :answer-field/id #uuid "58cd702c-0681-5a8b-9b37-effe51b705f8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391971}] :question/id #uuid "80225fd7-5e7b-5d9b-be48-77d560bf02e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-36357" :question/problem "Let $B={\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}}$ and $C={\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}}$ be bases of ${R}^{2}.$ Find the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ and $C$ as ${{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ and ${{c}_{1},{c}_{2}}$, respectively.\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$ is a matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors of $B$ relative to the basis $C.$\n\nHence, we need to find the coordinates of ${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2}$ relative to the basis $C.$ We can do this simultaneously by considering the matrix\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}| & | & | & | \\\\ {c}_{1} & {c}_{2} & {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} \\\\ | & | & | & |\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we simply reduce the left-hand side to reduced row-echelon form using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -4 & 6 & -7 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & -10\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & -10\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{2} & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the right-hand side, we obtain the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 7 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247359 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7cc97414-0741-5dcb-8a43-74df4bb4196e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245407} {:answer/id #uuid "9d1c74d1-9886-5ee6-94e9-df81c7cca410" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245711} {:answer/id #uuid "9e9bebec-3b58-5ac4-a53b-969cdd49744f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245728} {:answer/id #uuid "c85f6ce4-7995-55dc-8977-d78ad3c7c28f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246090} {:answer/id #uuid "ec51d526-cd38-520f-a996-d5e2aa4c6ba7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246404}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246404} :answer-field/id #uuid "17f129c9-21d6-537a-83eb-dc76f8f77b3e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246587}] :question/id #uuid "3b028c1b-2596-51e4-85c0-5cc2ad0dbfbc" :question/math-academy-id "q-113510" :question/problem "Let $B={\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}}$ and $C={\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}}$ be bases of ${R}^{2}.$ Find the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ and $C$ as ${{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ and ${{c}_{1},{c}_{2}}$, respectively.\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$ is a matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors of $B$ relative to the basis $C.$\n\nHence, we need to find the coordinates of ${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2}$ relative to the basis $C.$ We can do this simultaneously by considering the matrix\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}| & | & | & | \\\\ {c}_{1} & {c}_{2} & {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} \\\\ | & | & | & |\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we simply reduce the left-hand side to reduced row-echelon form using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 9 & 6\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 & -12\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the right-hand side, we obtain the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247362 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d256c9b-ca10-5ea9-a696-f3ed6a0a6b0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 16\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245135} {:answer/id #uuid "74e82f9c-7a8a-5418-962f-6a02b594b33e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 17\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245356} {:answer/id #uuid "a5603449-58ca-55fa-b9cf-370a1ffff990" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 4 & \\frac{1}{17}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245798} {:answer/id #uuid "e9322699-dec2-5ff2-921c-2b01f57dd42a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246380} {:answer/id #uuid "eda62fbe-9a7c-5138-b269-2ee24eacf510" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 17\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246412}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 17\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246412} :answer-field/id #uuid "a077ac69-607f-57ea-a0ce-e946298ab8c4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246829}] :question/id #uuid "cb921b26-a20c-5f23-a094-49ac99b2c6bd" :question/math-academy-id "q-113515" :question/problem "Let $B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}17 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\}$  be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and let $S$ be the standard basis of ${R}^{2}.$ Find the change-of-coordinates matrix from $S$ to $B.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ and $S$ as $\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ and $\\{{e}_{1},{e}_{2}\\}$, respectively. Recall that the standard basis of ${R}^{2}$ consists of the vectors\n\n$$\n{e}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{e}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $S$ to $B$ is a matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors of $S$ relative to the basis $B.$\n\nHence, we need to find the coordinates of ${e}_{1}$ and ${e}_{2}$ relative to the basis $B.$ We can do this simultaneously by considering the matrix\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}| & | & | & | \\\\ {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} & {e}_{1} & {e}_{2} \\\\ | & | & | & |\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we simply reduce the left-hand side to reduced row-echelon form using Gaussian elimination: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}17 & 4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{17}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & \\frac{4}{17} & \\frac{1}{17} & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & \\frac{4}{17} & \\frac{1}{17} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{17} & -\\frac{4}{17} & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=17{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & \\frac{4}{17} & \\frac{1}{17} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & 17\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-\\frac{4}{17}){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & 17\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the right-hand side, we obtain the change-of-coordinates matrix from $S$ to $B.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{P}_{S\\to B}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 17\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247363 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f3b02cb-d19b-5a2f-97f8-5c07740f7740" :an