s $C.$ We can do this simultaneously by considering the matrix\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}| & | & | & | \\\\ {c}_{1} & {c}_{2} & {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} \\\\ | & | & | & |\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we simply reduce the left-hand side to reduced row-echelon form using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 6 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 6 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & 6\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 6 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the right-hand side, we obtain the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323709 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1682459f-7e14-5c8b-b4dd-e25fbe6b9c97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321332} {:answer/id #uuid "49f0a7d6-37a9-5883-acc6-368c3161d137" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321728} {:answer/id #uuid "59159a55-bee5-5e72-8745-54d4a14ab2c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321850} {:answer/id #uuid "e28e0dac-b74b-5892-b4d7-357e0c93c1d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322916} {:answer/id #uuid "fad55dd9-6f24-57ad-a90f-15f24cb59c9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323125}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/r