0 \\\\ 2 & \\sqrt{2} & 7 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,Q=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,R=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A square matrix $A$ is symmetric if it is equal to its transpose:\n\n$$\nA={A}^{T}\n$$\n\nEquivalently, ${a}_{ij}={a}_{ji}$ for all $i,j.$ In other words, $A$ is symmetric across its main diagonal. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- $P$ is a symmetric matrix. Indeed, $P={P}^{T}.$\n\n- $Q$ is *not* a symmetric matrix. Since ${q}_{12}\\ne {q}_{21},$ we obtain $Q\\ne {Q}^{T}.$\n\n$$\nQ=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $R$ is a symmetric matrix. Indeed, $R={R}^{T}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$P$ and $R$ only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357613 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e79675c-d340-558d-85a1-f9f7b1029de9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469662} {:answer/id #uuid "60bd1f0c-8a39-5c12-8e0f-a94ebe34fcb1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469663}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469662} :answer-field/id #uuid "579a2afb-cfc8-5b6a-b249-9a478ce20513" :answer-field/key "P" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470443} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b879cd8-8163-5323-9891-635c9985bcba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469664} {:answer/id #uuid "607d0264-5580-5201-bc08-95e2af57eb0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469665}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469665} :answer-field/id #uuid "a537cbd9-73a4-5a02-9dd4-d84d4bc3cef5" :answe